    {
      "title": "1. Start here: the budgeting loop",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every method below is a way to run the same three-step loop. Get the loop right",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "first; the method is just packaging.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Know your income - total monthly take-home (net) pay, not gross. Use",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "pay stubs. (See §6 if income is irregular.)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Track your spending - log where money actually goes for at least a few",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "weeks before trusting any budget. Most people underestimate discretionary",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "spending until they see it. Start small (one week of receipts or one checking",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "account) if it feels overwhelming.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Plan and adjust - assign the income to categories, compare plan vs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "actual at month-end, and adjust. Income minus expenses should be ≥ 0; if",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "it's negative you're spending more than you make and need to cut, earn more,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A budget is simply a written plan for the money you expect each month. Its job",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "is to make sure money covers obligations and leaves room to save.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#1-start-here-the-budgeting-loop",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. The four budgeting methods — and when each fits",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "These are not exclusive. A common, durable combination: pay-yourself-first",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#2-the-four-budgeting-methods-and-when-each-fits",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "to automate savings off the top, run the rest as a zero-based plan, and use",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#2-the-four-budgeting-methods-and-when-each-fits",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "envelopes only on the one or two categories that tend to overspend.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#2-the-four-budgeting-methods-and-when-each-fits",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Tracking spending",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Pick a capture method you'll actually keep up with: a notebook/journal, a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "receipts-in-a-folder review at week's end, a spreadsheet, or an app that",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "auto-imports transactions. Consistency beats sophistication.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Categorize (housing, utilities, groceries, transportation, dining,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "entertainment, etc.) so you can see patterns, then compare to your plan.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The CFPB publishes free, no-login Spending Tracker and **Budget",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Worksheet** tools (see References) that do this on paper or PDF.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Review plan vs. actual monthly. The point of tracking isn't guilt - it's",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "finding the one or two categories where small changes free up real money.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#3-tracking-spending",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. SMART financial goals & the federal frame",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Vague goals (\"save more\") fail. Make each goal SMART: Specific,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound - e.g., \"save",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "$1,200 for a starter emergency fund by saving $100/month for 12 months.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The federal Financial Literacy and Education Commission (FLEC) frames money",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "management around the MyMoney Five (a useful checklist behind any budget):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "EARN - understand pay and benefits.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "SAVE & INVEST - start early, even in small amounts.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PROTECT - emergency savings + appropriate insurance.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "SPEND - get value; comparison-shop big purchases.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "BORROW - credit can enable purchases but interest is a cost.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(Investing and insurance are only named here; their mechanics live in sibling",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "skills - see the SKIP list.)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#4-smart-financial-goals-the-federal-frame",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sinking funds",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A sinking fund is a planned savings bucket for a **known, irregular,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#sinking-funds",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "non-monthly expense** - car registration, holidays, annual insurance premiums,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#sinking-funds",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "a replacement laptop. Divide the expected cost by months until due and save that",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#sinking-funds",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "slice each month. This converts \"surprise\" expenses into ordinary line items and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#sinking-funds",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "is the single best defense against raiding the emergency fund for things that",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#sinking-funds",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "weren't actually emergencies.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#sinking-funds",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Emergency fund",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The cushion that keeps a job loss, car repair, or medical bill from becoming",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "credit-card debt. This is the PROTECT piece of any budget.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "How much: the common rule of thumb is 3-6 months of essential expenses",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(housing, utilities, food, insurance, minimum debt payments, transportation) —",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "not 3-6 months of income. CFPB itself sets no fixed dollar figure and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "stresses that even a small amount provides security; a widely used",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "starter goal is $500-$1,000 (or one month of expenses) before building",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "toward the full 3-6 months.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Lean toward the higher end (6+ months) with variable/self-employed",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "income, a single income supporting dependents, or specialized job markets;",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "the lower end is reasonable with very stable dual incomes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Where to keep it: somewhere safe and liquid but slightly inconvenient",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "to spend - separate from your everyday checking. A **high-yield savings",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "account (HYSA)** or money market account at a bank or credit union is the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "typical home (account mechanics, APY, and FDIC/NCUA insurance live in the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "personal-banking sibling). The emergency fund is not an investment —",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "don't put it in stocks where it can drop right when you need it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Starting when money is tight: manage cash-flow timing (align bill due",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "dates to paydays; many billers will move a due date), and **capture",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "windfalls** - route all or part of a tax refund, bonus, or cash gift straight",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#5-emergency-fund",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Budgeting on irregular / variable income",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Gig work, commissions, tips, seasonal or self-employment income break the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "fixed-paycheck assumption. The fix is to **budget on a conservative baseline and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Find a baseline. Average net income over the last 6-12 months, or - safer",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "— budget to your lowest recent month so essentials are always covered.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cover essentials first. Rank fixed/essential costs; the baseline must",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "cover those before any discretionary spending.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use a buffer / \"income-smoothing\" account. In good months, park the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "surplus above baseline; in lean months, top up to baseline from it. This",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "evens out the lumps. (This buffer is separate from the emergency fund.)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Make savings a percentage, not a flat dollar amount, so it scales with a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "big month instead of getting skipped in a small one.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Set aside taxes if self-employed (no employer withholding) - the tax-form",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mechanics belong to a tax skill, but the budgeting habit is to quarantine a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "percentage of every payment immediately.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#6-budgeting-on-irregular-variable-income",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Automating savings (make it the default)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Automation removes willpower from the equation and operationalizes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "pay-yourself-first:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Automatic recurring transfers from checking to savings, timed just after",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "payday (even $25-$50 per paycheck compounds into a real fund).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Split direct deposit: ask your employer to route a fixed amount or",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "percentage of each paycheck straight into savings so it never lands in",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Auto-escalate: raise the transfer amount when income rises or a debt is",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "paid off, so freed-up cash is redirected rather than absorbed by lifestyle.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Automate sinking-fund contributions the same way, one transfer per bucket",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(or one bucket with a tracking spreadsheet).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#7-automating-savings-make-it-the-default",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Debt-payoff methods: snowball vs. avalanche",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Two structured ways to attack multiple debts. In both, you pay **minimums on",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "everything and throw every extra dollar at one target debt**; when it's",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "gone, you roll that freed-up payment onto the next (the \"snowball\" rolling",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "effect). They differ only in which debt is the target:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Which to pick: the avalanche is mathematically optimal, but the *best plan",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "is the one you'll actually finish*. If motivation is the bottleneck, the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "snowball's early wins are worth a little extra interest. A hybrid (knock out one",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "tiny balance for a quick win, then switch to avalanche) is common.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Scope line: this is about paying off debt you can afford to pay. If a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> debt is in collections, charged off, or you're considering settling for less",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> than owed (and the 1099-C tax hit), see",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> charge-offs-collections-and-debt-resolution. If a collector is",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> contacting or suing you, see debt-collectors-and-fdcpa-rights. A formal",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> debt management plan (DMP) through a counselor is covered in §10.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#8-debt-payoff-methods-snowball-vs-avalanche",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. Budgeting tools & apps landscape (tool-neutral)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The post-Mint shift: Intuit's free Mint app - long the default",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "free aggregator - was shut down in early 2024 (Intuit steered users to",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Credit Karma, which lacks Mint's budgeting tools), pushing users to",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "alternatives. The current landscape is a mix of",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "subscription apps (e.g., zero-based/envelope-style and aggregator tools),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "free bank/credit-union built-in budgeting dashboards, spreadsheets,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and paper/PDF worksheets. This skill stays tool-neutral - pick by",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "method fit and privacy comfort, not brand.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Pick by the method you'll run: want every dollar assigned → a zero-based",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "app or template; want hard category limits → an envelope/cash-stuffing app;",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "just want awareness → an aggregator or your bank's dashboard or a tracker",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Privacy matters with aggregators. Apps that link to your accounts pull",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "sensitive transaction data; the **CFPB has flagged that many financial apps",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "collect and share user data with third parties** (data brokers, advertisers).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Read the data-sharing terms, prefer providers with clear limits, and note",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "that a spreadsheet or paper system shares nothing. (The CFPB's own free tools",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "don't collect what you enter.)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "You don't need an app at all. A spreadsheet or the free CFPB Budget",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Worksheet + Spending Tracker runs every method above.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#9-budgeting-tools-apps-landscape-tool-neutral",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "10. Free help",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Budgeting help is widely available at no cost - you should not pay an up-front",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "fee for basic budgeting or counseling:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Nonprofit credit counseling. Member agencies of the **National Foundation",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "for Credit Counseling (NFCC) offer a free initial counseling session**: a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "certified counselor reviews your full budget and debts and builds an action",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "plan. If credit-card debt is the problem, they can set up a **debt management",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "plan (DMP) - you make one monthly payment** to the agency, which",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "distributes it to creditors, typically paying off cards over 3-5 years,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "often at reduced rates. Choose an NFCC-accredited agency.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Financial coaching. Free/low-cost coaching is offered through many",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "nonprofits, employers (financial-wellness benefits), credit unions,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "libraries, and military programs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Federal resources. MyMoney.gov (the FLEC portal) and the CFPB",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "publish free, vendor-neutral guides, worksheets, and the *Your Money, Your",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Goals* toolkit. AnnualCreditReport.com for free credit reports relates to",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "the credit-score siblings, not budgeting.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "**Avoid \"debt relief\" or \"credit repair\" outfits that demand large up-front",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "fees** or promise to erase debts - those are a different (and riskier)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "category; legitimate nonprofit counseling starts free.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/budgeting-and-saving/#10-free-help",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
